<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wakayama Prefecture</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wakayama">Wakayama</a> Prefecture is a prefecture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> in the Kansai region, covering the western and southern part of the Kii Peninsula, with its capital at Wakayama. It was created in 1871 from the Kii domain when the domains were abolished. Largely mountainous, it includes the sacred sites of Kōyasan and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kumano">Kumano</a> and is known for mandarin oranges, plums and fishing.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wakayama-prefecture.jpg" alt="Wakayama Prefecture" width="320" height="229" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Big Ben in Japan · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pagoda_and_Nachi_Falls_2017-10-12.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
